 Tested versions\n\nOccurs on:\n- v4.4.beta1.mono.official [d33da79d3]\n\nDoes not occur on:\n- v4.4.dev7.mono.official [46c8f8c5c]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.beta1.mono - SteamOS holo on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - integrated AMD Custom GPU 0405 (RADV VANGOGH) - AMD Custom APU 0405 (8 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen the disabled property on CollisionShape3D is set from false to true while using Jolt Physics, any collision that happens shortly after will spam the area_entered signal. \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Enable Jolt Physics from the Project Settings (Physics>3D)\n2. Add multiple Area3D nodes with CollisionShape3D nodes as children (Mesh3D as well for visibility)\n3. Add a script that will move the shapes through each other\n4. Run the project\n5. During runtime, toggle the Disabled property on the CollisionShape3D in the inspector\n\nNote: You can script the disabled toggle behaviour as well, but through the inspector is how I reproduce it in the test project.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[CollisionShape3DDisabledPropertyJolt.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18456599/CollisionShape3DDisabledPropertyJolt.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com